c. Suggest a product solution for the most severe bug you've found
In my opinion, the most severe issue visible in this mock-up is the lack of support for international billing addresses.
For a global SaaS company, this is not just a usability problem. It is a business issue that could lead to lost customers and revenue.
My suggestion would be to make the billing form dynamic based on the customer's country.
I would add a Country dropdown at the beginning of the billing address section. Once the customer selects a country, the form should display the relevant address fields and validation rules.
For example, US customers would see State and ZIP Code fields, Israeli customers would be able to enter their local postal code, and customers from other countries would see the appropriate address format.
I would also make sure the payment currency, total amount, applicable taxes, and billing frequency are clearly displayed.
Rather than building and maintaining all the payment and international address logic from scratch, I would recommend using an established payment provider that supports international payments.
This would improve the user experience, reduce payment failures, and help the company avoid unnecessary security